{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"scholarly-petite-taruca","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Container eval fixtures without a `children` payload cannot be run by `run_case`\n\n## Problem\n\n`eval_solver._run_criterion_case` raises for a CONTAINER criterion (G3 / G4 / decomp-shape) whose\ncase carries no non-empty `children` list -- the criterion runs over a (parent, children,\nsibling-roster) decomposition, not inline text. Several `plan-review-container.eval.yaml` cases\ncarry only `input` (the parent plan) and no `children`, so they cannot be executed through\n`run_case` at all. `plan-review-decomp-shape.eval.yaml` cases DO carry `children`.\n\n## Evidence (measured, story 0d76)\n\nIn the live provider-parity run, `G3-R-uncovered-ac-rebar` and\n`G3-FP-covered-by-named-consumer-rebar` raised\n`ValueError: container criterion 'G3' needs a non-empty children list in the eval fixture` on\nBOTH arms at ALL 3 epochs, before any model call, on both class slots. They contributed nothing\nbut error counts. `provider_parity._runnable` now excludes them, so the parity corpus is 28\nitems rather than 30 -- but the underlying fixtures remain unrunnable through this path.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Decide whether these container cases should gain a `children` payload (making them runnable\n      and restoring them to the parity corpus) or be documented as runnable only through\n      `pass1_container` directly.\n- [ ] If payloads are added, `provider_parity.eligible_cases` picks them up with no code change\n      and the corpus returns to 30 items.\n","id":"3e8b-3c65-80ad-4673","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"container eval fixtures lack the children payload run_case needs"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785716455049848001,"uuid":"e65f8ade-f8a2-4bfc-be49-ea94e6dde019"}